{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-bf879a43929ba8d6", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# How Contrastive Decoding Enhances Large Audio Language Models?\narXiv: 2603.09232\nAuthors: Tzu-Quan Lin, Wei-Ping Huang, Yi-Cheng Lin, Hung-yi Lee\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We verify that contrastive decoding enhances multi-token generation in Large Audio Language Models, extending beyond prior applications limited to single-token classification.\n  2. We identify Audio-Aware Decoding and Audio Contrastive Decoding as the most effective contrastive decoding strategies for Large Audio Language Models.\n  3. We demonstrate that the magnitude of improvement from contrastive decoding is highly dependent on the underlying model architecture.\n  4. We establish that contrastive decoding reliably corrects errors related to audio blindness and guessing, but fails to rectify errors stemming from flawed reasoning or confident misassertions.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/理解型\n===NEXT===\n# A Survey on Audio Diffusion Models: Text To Speech Synthesis and Enhancement in Generative AI\narXiv: 2303.13336\nAuthors: Chenshuang Zhang, Chaoning Zhang, Sheng Zheng, Mengchun Zhang, Maryam Qamar, Sung-Ho Bae, In So Kweon\nYear: 2023 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Provides the first comprehensive survey specifically focused on recent progress in diffusion-based speech synthesis.\n  2. Categorizes text-to-speech diffusion methods into three distinct groups based on the model stage: acoustic model, vocoder, and end-to-end framework.\n  3. Classifies speech enhancement tasks into two types depending on whether specific signals are removed from or added to the input speech.\n  4. Includes comparisons of experimental results and detailed discussions across the reviewed methods.\n\nTags: TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, Vocoder/Diffusion\n===NEXT===\n# CosyVoice: A Scalable Multilingual Zero-shot Text-to-speech Synthesizer based on Supervised Semantic Tokens\narXiv: 2407.05407\nAuthors: Zhihao Du, Qian Chen, Shiliang Zhang, Kai Hu, Heng Lu, Yexin Yang, Hangrui Hu, Siqi Zheng, Yue Gu, Ziyang Ma, Zhifu Gao, Zhijie Yan\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We are the first to integrate supervised speech tokens into text-to-speech models, enhancing content consistency and speaker similarity in zero-shot voice cloning.\n  2. We propose CosyVoice, a scalable zero-shot TTS synthesis system that combines an LLM for text-to-token generation with a conditional flow matching model for token-to-speech synthesis, forsaking the need for additional phonemizers and forced aligners.\n  3. We refine the quality of generated speech by incorporating the x-vector into the LLM to separate speech modeling into semantic, speaker, and prosody components, and optimize the flow matching process with classifier-free guidance, a cosine scheduler, and masked conditions.\n\nTags: TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多语言, TTS/功能-多说话人, 压缩/监督-有监督, 压缩/语义声学-语义", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "39a64380-dcef-4470-b4e4-3045cb700a86", "uuid": "17ae69a6-da81-46b9-9418-43cbd40eecff", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T20:47:09.242Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# How Contrastive Decoding Enhances Large Audio Language Models?\narXiv: 2603.09232\nAuthors: Tzu-Quan Lin, Wei-Ping Huang, Yi-Cheng Lin, Hung-yi Lee\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We verify that contrastive decoding enhances multi-token generation in Large Audio Language Models, extending beyond prior applications limited to single-token classification.\n  2. We identify Audio-Aware Decoding and Audio Contrastive Decoding as the most effective contrastive decoding strategies for Large Audio Language Models.\n  3. We demonstrate that the magnitude of improvement from contrastive decoding is highly dependent on the underlying model architecture.\n  4. We establish that contrastive decoding reliably corrects errors related to audio blindness and guessing, but fails to rectify errors stemming from flawed reasoning or confident misassertions.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/理解型\n===NEXT===\n# A Survey on Audio Diffusion Models: Text To Speech Synthesis and Enhancement in Generative AI\narXiv: 2303.13336\nAuthors: Chenshuang Zhang, Chaoning Zhang, Sheng Zheng, Mengchun Zhang, Maryam Qamar, Sung-Ho Bae, In So Kweon\nYear: 2023 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Provides the first comprehensive survey specifically focused on recent progress in diffusion-based speech synthesis.\n  2. Categorizes text-to-speech diffusion methods into three distinct groups based on the model stage: acoustic model, vocoder, and end-to-end framework.\n  3. Classifies speech enhancement tasks into two types depending on whether specific signals are removed from or added to the input speech.\n  4. Includes comparisons of experimental results and detailed discussions across the reviewed methods.\n\nTags: TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, Vocoder/Diffusion\n===NEXT===\n# CosyVoice: A Scalable Multilingual Zero-shot Text-to-speech Synthesizer based on Supervised Semantic Tokens\narXiv: 2407.05407\nAuthors: Zhihao Du, Qian Chen, Shiliang Zhang, Kai Hu, Heng Lu, Yexin Yang, Hangrui Hu, Siqi Zheng, Yue Gu, Ziyang Ma, Zhifu Gao, Zhijie Yan\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We are the first to integrate supervised speech tokens into text-to-speech models, enhancing content consistency and speaker similarity in zero-shot voice cloning.\n  2. We propose CosyVoice, a scalable zero-shot TTS synthesis system that combines an LLM for text-to-token generation with a conditional flow matching model for token-to-speech synthesis, forsaking the need for additional phonemizers and forced aligners.\n  3. We refine the quality of generated speech by incorporating the x-vector into the LLM to separate speech modeling into semantic, speaker, and prosody components, and optimize the flow matching process with classifier-free guidance, a cosine scheduler, and masked conditions.\n\nTags: TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多语言, TTS/功能-多说话人, 压缩/监督-有监督, 压缩/语义声学-语义", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
